Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 21:53:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03905/11362] [outer-loop] goal-free L1->L2 probe: VALID NULL
 on lp85 + the alignment reframe

proto_goalfree_deepen: both arms reach lp85 L1 reproducibly (3/3) but NEITHER
reaches L2, with the Go-Explore archive genuinely exercised (232 prefix injections
after the _frame_grid fix) -> a VALID null (not a false negative; positive control +
lever-exercised both pass; adversarial_verify clean).

Two findings: (1) the Go-Explore _frame_grid bug meant the conductor's .433 A2
tested a DEAD archive -- its null is suspect. (2) lp85's L2 is goal-DIRECTED
(marker_pair_shape_alignment: align each piece to its goal sprite), so goal-free
exploration cannot solve it by construction -- the null is expected, and it
de-justifies the CNN-driver build for lp85 + redirects the next step to a
PERCEPTION-GROUNDED structural-alignment goal (detect pieces+sprites, goal = aligned)
built on the .433 A1 object-centric perception -- NOT another exemplar-replay variant
(that's why single-exemplar nulled: a flat grid can't express the alignment goal).

